  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because the premise doesn't hold for the `OrderPlaced` event.\n\n`contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` shows `analytics-ingest` (deployed version 3) requires `channel` on `OrderPlaced`, as `enum:web|store|marketplace`. If I removed the field from the event, `npm run verify-contracts` (`scripts/verify-contracts.mjs`) would fail. More importantly, the deployed consumer would likely break.\n\nRemoving `channel` from the order model would also remove the source for the event field, so the two changes can't be separated.\n\nHere are some ways to proceed:\n1. **Keep the event field and remove it later.** Update `analytics-ingest` to stop requiring `channel` and deploy it. Then update its contract file and remove `channel` from the event and the model. I can do the code side once the contract is updated.\n2. **Remove it from the model and API input only.** The event would have to keep sending some `channel` value, which needs a source for it. That seems to defeat the purpose.\n3. **Go ahead anyway.** If you know `analytics-ingest` is already migrated and the contract file is just stale, tell me. I'll remove the field everywhere, including `src/core/order.ts`, `events.ts`, `requestParsing.ts`, the tests, the docs, and the contract file.\n\nWhich of these do you want?",
